  "name": "Bèlè (Martinique drum-dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Afro-Martinican drum-dance centred on the north Atlantic coast around Sainte-Marie, in which a lead singer and the lavwa chorus answer each other over the tanbou bèlè, played by a drummer seated astride it, while the tibwa player beats two sticks on the drum's body; dancers perform in quadrille-like sets of couples. Its family of dances includes bèlè, gran bèlè, bèlè linò and kalennda, and a late-twentieth-century revival brought it back into community swaré bèlè; the palitos card stands in for the tibwa.",
